 "name": "Autumn Forest Canopy Gaps – Drone Photo Beauty Rating",
 "description": "Faithful replication of Li et al. (2021), \"Canopy Gaps Improve Landscape Aesthetic Service by Promoting Autumn Color-Leaved Tree Species Diversity and Color-Leaved Patch Properties in Subalpine Forests of Southwestern China\", Forests 12:199. Participants answer five background questions (gender, residence, age, occupation, education) and then rate 21 drone photographs (~50 m above each plot) of subalpine autumn colour-leaved forest plots in Li County, western Sichuan, on the original 7-point scale (3 like very much … -3 dislike very much). The original study collected 219 online questionnaires (179 valid) and used the standardised scores as the landscape aesthetic service (LAS) of each plot; the number and total area of canopy gaps, especially medium gaps (51–100 m²), raised LAS by increasing colour-leaved patch area.\n\nPhotographs and questionnaire wording: Li et al. (2021), Supporting Information Appendix S1, CC BY 4.0. Used with credit for research; the template is removed if the authors object.\n\nDifferences from the original study: (1) English only (the original was a Chinese online questionnaire on Wenjuanxing); (2) photos are the 689-px versions printed in the supplement, not the original drone files; (3) a consent checkbox was added; (4) the original removed respondents who gave the same answer to every photo, which is left to the analysis here.",
